  "_comment": "Golden wire shape for the NEW export GET /api/v1/management/licensing/agents/export?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD (L9 + L10), application/json, PlatformAdminOnly; the owner attaches it (or its chainHeads) to the monthly self-declaration. events[] = license_agent_events rows (append-only), daily[] = license_agent_daily rows INCLUDING every correction revision, both in their per-tenant chain order (sequence ascending). One hash chain per tenant spans its events AND daily rows (shared sequence); rows with tenantId null are the deployment chain (deployment daily totals plus its own anchor rows). rowHash = 'lac1:' + hex(SHA-256(prevHash | canonical fields)); the first row of a chain is kind chain_anchored, whose prevHash is the genesis 'lac1:' + hex(SHA-256('genesis' | tenantId-or-'deployment' | licenseId)). A licence change (renewal, PUT /license hot swap, revalidation) appends chain_reanchored with the new licenseId, linked to the old head, never a new genesis. kind is one of: chain_anchored, chain_reanchored, agent_baseline (one per agent row that already exists when a tenant chain is first anchored), agent_created, agent_deleted, user_status_changed, user_deleted, conversation_taken_over, conversation_transferred, conversation_reassigned. userStatus is Active|Suspended|Deactivated (null when not a user_status_changed or user_deleted row; for user_deleted it is the last status). counted is the post-event countability of agentId (agent row exists AND its user is Active), null for chain rows. daily[].closedThroughSequence is the highest event sequence of that chain the close had seen; an event with a higher sequence whose occurredAt falls inside an already-closed day triggers a correction row (revision + 1). Timestamps are UTC ISO-8601; day is a date in dayZone. The ledger stores ids only (no names or e-mails). Every child change's delta spec must cite these field names VERBATIM (verbatim-fixture-citation rule, /xr:propagate).",
